<p>Alright, well, there's certainly a <em>lot</em> here, which is definitely something. It's definitely a lot to get through.</p>
<p>My problem with this piece is the dialogue. I don't really know how to expand on this, so suffice to say that I don't really buy it. The things they're saying don't really meet the bar, I feel.</p>
<p>Here's one example that I think is sort of indicative of the entire piece, and while it's probably not the <em>most</em> problematic few lines in the article, it's definitely not super.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Zimmerman:</strong> I don't. Toss and turn every night. See a lot of faces, people I've killed, [Cough.] people who've died. But it's not as tough when you realize you're suffering [Cough.] so billions of others can sleep without thinking about anything but their boring lives.</p>
<p>[Silence.]</p>
<p><strong>Zimmerman:</strong> We die in the dark, so they can live in the light.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Especially that last line&#8230; it feels like a script someone in the fan community might write for an SCP movie. There is no part of me that believes for even a moment that real people would ever talk like that.</p>
<p>There are a lot of examples of this, but honestly it's just too long to go through and name them all. I can tell you put a lot of work into this and I admire the effort, but too much of this article relies on the interactions between these characters to just ignore this. It's so hard to get through sometimes because I'm being pulled out of the article so frequently.</p>
<p>I don't know what I'd recommend to fix that issue - all I can say is that in its current form, for me, it's not really there.</p>

